```yara
import "pe"

/*
    Template for matching the confirmed RedLine sample set represented by
    the analyst-extracted indicators below.

    This rule is not intended to establish family attribution. Validate new
    matches before associating them with RedLine or deploying automated action.
*/
rule SOC_Confirmed_SampleSet_RedLine_Credential_Stealer
{
    meta:
        description = "Detects a confirmed credential-stealer sample set using analyst-extracted PE and string indicators"
        author = "SOC Detection Engineering"
        date = "2026-07-31"
        scope = "Confirmed sample set only; not a family-level attribution rule"
        reference = "TODO: internal case or analysis reference"
        sample_sha256 = "TODO: confirmed sample SHA-256"
        confidence = "high for known samples; unknown for broader family coverage"

    strings:
        // Windows DPAPI function commonly used to decrypt stored credentials.
        $api_dpapi = "CryptUnprotectData" ascii wide

        // SQLite function associated with opening browser or application databases.
        $api_sqlite = "sqlite3_open" ascii wide

    condition:
        // Require a valid PE structure with enough sections for both checks.
        pe.is_pe and
        pe.number_of_sections >= 2 and

        // Both analyst-extracted strings must be present.
        all of ($api_*) and

        // Require the expected executable-code section.
        for any i in (0..pe.number_of_sections - 1) : (
            pe.sections[i].name == ".text"
        ) and

        // Require the expected read-only data section.
        for any i in (0..pe.number_of_sections - 1) : (
            pe.sections[i].name == ".rdata"
        )
}
```

The scope metadata and comments deliberately limit the rule to the confirmed sample set rather than claiming general RedLine family coverage.

